(6990811, 1055964, 43463, '<td valign="top">Within these walls are the voices of those long past. From time to time their spirits manifest and walk the halls. They are silent - never keening, never shrill. Malicious they are not, they just are a ghost of their former selves.<br/> <br/>Great color, clarity and mood in this capture.</td>', 'Within these walls are the voices of those long past. From time to time their spirits manifest and walk the halls. They are silent - never keening, never shrill. Malicious they are not, they just are a ghost of their former selves. Great color, clarity and mood in this capture.', '2013-03-04 09:09:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990814, 1056026, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>Great capture! Love the smile on the boy and the baby snuggled with the giant teddy bear is adorable. Great lighting and fabulous composition of subjects - this is a wonderful children''s portrait.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  Great capture! Love the smile on the boy and the baby snuggled with the giant teddy bear is adorable. Great lighting and fabulous composition of subjects - this is a wonderful children''s portrait.', '2013-03-04 09:12:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990817, 1053444, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Fabulous lighting, color and detail in this floral shot. Love the glow on the background for it makes the orchid glow; thus taking center stage. The teardrop coming off center petal is that little extra detail that makes this floral shot stand out.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Fabulous lighting, color and detail in this floral shot. Love the glow on the background for it makes the orchid glow; thus taking center stage. The teardrop coming off center petal is that little extra detail that makes this floral shot stand out.', '2013-03-04 09:17:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990821, 1055996, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I think why I find this most appealing is the texture and the mood captured. The blue crackle backdrop both in color and overall feel gives me the sense of a cold, blustery day - the kind where the air is so crisp it crackles. The branches/willowy weed/flowers adds to the scene in that I see and ''feel'' that cold wind rushing through - blowing the foliage making it bend and reach.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I think why I find this most appealing is the texture and the mood captured. The blue crackle backdrop both in color and overall feel gives me the sense of a cold, blustery day - the kind where the air is so crisp it crackles. The branches/willowy weed/flowers adds to the scene in that I see and ''feel'' that cold wind rushing through - blowing the foliage making it bend and reach.', '2013-03-04 09:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990827, 1055769, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>The B&amp;W tones are fabulous. It captures the action of the girl''s singing quite well, but it seems too distant and at first glance there seems nothing more to the picture. Those who choose to linger will spot an interesting counterpoint to the joyful singing in the sullen girl in the top left. As I mentioned before that it seemed distant - it is because I think you need to bring us closer to the ''action'' - draw us in closer to the element of the story you wish to tell. Here it gets lost in a sea of girls. A closer crop and a square crop will bring the viewer in for a closer more personal look and feel.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. The B&W tones are fabulous. It captures the action of the girl''s singing quite well, but it seems too distant and at first glance there seems nothing more to the picture. Those who choose to linger will spot an interesting counterpoint to the joyful singing in the sullen girl in the top left. As I mentioned before that it seemed distant - it is because I think you need to bring us closer to the ''action'' - draw us in closer to the element of the story you wish to tell. Here it gets lost in a sea of girls. A closer crop and a square crop will bring the viewer in for a closer more personal look and feel.', '2013-03-04 09:30:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990831, 1056003, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love the motion blur shown in this fencing match (a foil I believe from what little I can see of the handle and blade). That blur adds to the sense of action going on. I think it would improve the composition if both the blade and the helmet were in better focus...and perhaps a tad bit more focus detail on the fencer on the left as well. The detail is there on the blade and the legs of the lunging fencer, but it just needs a little more on the helmet/head. It is a difficult thing to get the right amount of motion blur to show the action balanced with the right amount of focus on the subjects to showcase some detail, but I believe with that perfect balance this would take this from a good shot to an excellent shot.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love the motion blur shown in this fencing match (a foil I believe from what little I can see of the handle and blade). That blur adds to the sense of action going on. I think it would improve the composition if both the blade and the helmet were in better focus...and perhaps a tad bit more focus detail on the fencer on the left as well. The detail is there on the blade and the legs of the lunging fencer, but it just needs a little more on the helmet/head. It is a difficult thing to get the right amount of motion blur to show the action balanced with the right amount of focus on the subjects to showcase some detail, but I believe with that perfect balance this would take this from a good shot to an excellent shot.', '2013-03-04 09:38:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990836, 1055999, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>B&amp;W tones are great. Interesting street capture of the everyday with something a little extraordinary - the snow. While this is a good street photography shot it needs that extra something to make it more compelling for the viewer to stop and linger awhile to take in the scene. I am finding it difficult to find an element that is the main subject of the shot. If the woman by the flowers was holding one up and inspecting it - that action would be different from the rest of the scene thus drawing our eye into her and her actions being the main subject of the composition.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. B&W tones are great. Interesting street capture of the everyday with something a little extraordinary - the snow. While this is a good street photography shot it needs that extra something to make it more compelling for the viewer to stop and linger awhile to take in the scene. I am finding it difficult to find an element that is the main subject of the shot. If the woman by the flowers was holding one up and inspecting it - that action would be different from the rest of the scene thus drawing our eye into her and her actions being the main subject of the composition.', '2013-03-04 09:43:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990838, 1055459, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>What absolutely wonderful lighting that captures the look and feel of Tess singing on stage. Love the action and the detail captured in this shot.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. What absolutely wonderful lighting that captures the look and feel of Tess singing on stage. Love the action and the detail captured in this shot.', '2013-03-04 09:45:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990840, 1054711, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>While the rest of the environment is in sharp focus and detail the people are not. The people are surreal in a real world room. There are the common everyday objects of the tub, the chair, the windows and the mirror but amoung them are the uncommon/blurred objects - people. The everyday objects are static and still - the man &amp; woman are not they are in motion placing them in a different realm. The nude woman seems to hold the mirror like a shield, hiding/protecting herself from the man captured within. The reflection of the man stands within the confines of the mirror and takes on the errie aspect of a lurker. He is faceless and not in sharp detail - while not in the room he adds a sense of tension as we know not what the intentions or actions will be that follows.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. While the rest of the environment is in sharp focus and detail the people are not. The people are surreal in a real world room. There are the common everyday objects of the tub, the chair, the windows and the mirror but amoung them are the uncommon/blurred objects - people. The everyday objects are static and still - the man & woman are not they are in motion placing them in a different realm. The nude woman seems to hold the mirror like a shield, hiding/protecting herself from the man captured within. The reflection of the man stands within the confines of the mirror and takes on the errie aspect of a lurker. He is faceless and not in sharp detail - while not in the room he adds a sense of tension as we know not what the intentions or actions will be that follows.', '2013-03-04 09:54:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6990846, 1054950, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>You have many good elements here but it just needs a bit better lighting and a little bit more on the composition placement. First off the lighting is a bit flat that it doesn''t allow the tulip to visually pop off that yellow backdrop. Better lighting would add more defining highlights, shadows and tones that are different from the backdrop (one light from above at a 45 degree angle, and one from a below at a 45 degree angle both shining at the head and stem of the flower is what I would try). As it is now, the yellow tones of the tulip in some areas blend in so well with the tones of the backdrop. Second the compositional placement is good but could be a tad better. I like that you have the head of the flower in the bottom left corner in the composition but to create visual symmetry and a pleasing balance to the eye you need to place/get the stem to arise out of the bottom right corner.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. You have many good elements here but it just needs a bit better lighting and a little bit more on the composition placement. First off the lighting is a bit flat that it doesn''t allow the tulip to visually pop off that yellow backdrop. Better lighting would add more defining highlights, shadows and tones that are different from the backdrop (one light from above at a 45 degree angle, and one from a below at a 45 degree angle both shining at the head and stem of the flower is what I would try). As it is now, the yellow tones of the tulip in some areas blend in so well with the tones of the backdrop. Second the compositional placement is good but could be a tad better. I like that you have the head of the flower in the bottom left corner in the composition but to create visual symmetry and a pleasing balance to the eye you need to place/get the stem to arise out of the bottom right corner.', '2013-03-04 10:04:27.000000', NULL, 1),
