(6992172, 1055964, 123612, '<td valign="top">Fantastic!</td>', 'Fantastic!', '2013-03-05 14:49:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992199, 1055181, 138630, '<td valign="top">Bet this was a thrill to see - or maybe you have foxes visit often?  Such a beautiful animal.  Voted earlier.</td>', 'Bet this was a thrill to see - or maybe you have foxes visit often?  Such a beautiful animal.  Voted earlier.', '2013-03-05 15:06:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992202, 1054307, 138630, '<td valign="top">Excellent detail - must be a lake nearby :)  Voted earlier.</td>', 'Excellent detail - must be a lake nearby :)  Voted earlier.', '2013-03-05 15:06:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992203, 1055130, 138630, '<td valign="top">Beautiful tones and light and I love the lines of the stone walls leading us into and across the frame.  Voted earlier.</td>', 'Beautiful tones and light and I love the lines of the stone walls leading us into and across the frame.  Voted earlier.', '2013-03-05 15:07:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992205, 1056023, 138630, '<td valign="top">Great display, not only of the wings but also of the flying water droplets.  Voted earlier.</td>', 'Great display, not only of the wings but also of the flying water droplets.  Voted earlier.', '2013-03-05 15:08:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992220, 1055763, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Holy moly these insects are huge! I knew about Weta''s from the logo for Weta Workshop, but the size - well that is as close as I would want to be to one. You captured some nice sharp detail from the ''spikes'' on the back legs to the head and antennae. My only critique is that the ground plane is too busy and dark in tones to really allow this bug to stand out from the backdrop. It looks like you may have been holding the piece of bark with the Weta on it - it might have been better to raise it up and take a shot with the sky as the backdrop. The sky with it''s lighter tones would have allowed the dark tones of the insect to stand out and contrast more. Although....you may not have wanted to move it too much for it might take off in your direction &lt;shudder&gt; :-)</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Holy moly these insects are huge! I knew about Weta''s from the logo for Weta Workshop, but the size - well that is as close as I would want to be to one. You captured some nice sharp detail from the ''spikes'' on the back legs to the head and antennae. My only critique is that the ground plane is too busy and dark in tones to really allow this bug to stand out from the backdrop. It looks like you may have been holding the piece of bark with the Weta on it - it might have been better to raise it up and take a shot with the sky as the backdrop. The sky with it''s lighter tones would have allowed the dark tones of the insect to stand out and contrast more. Although....you may not have wanted to move it too much for it might take off in your direction <shudder> :-)', '2013-03-05 15:30:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992227, 1055974, 43463, '<td valign="top">Coming back to comment and bump up.<br/> <br/>Color and details are great. You captured some great details in that I can see the textures on the beak and the ''pitted/ripples'' in the white patch area  near the the eye. The lower 1/4 of the shot is not in as sharp focus I think that you could crop that out and made this look like a widescreen shot. Not only would it take away the soft focus area but the long rectangle shape of the composition would complement match that of the long head of the crane.</td>', 'Coming back to comment and bump up. Color and details are great. You captured some great details in that I can see the textures on the beak and the ''pitted/ripples'' in the white patch area  near the the eye. The lower 1/4 of the shot is not in as sharp focus I think that you could crop that out and made this look like a widescreen shot. Not only would it take away the soft focus area but the long rectangle shape of the composition would complement match that of the long head of the crane.', '2013-03-05 15:38:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992267, 1055963, 108580, '<td valign="top">Wonderful and engaging eyes caught. Boring into my soul! <br/>I''d say this was the same bird as another mouse catching entry. Perhaps not as powerful a shot but still technically very good in trying conditions. Wildlife needs to be rewarded especially when we go to these lengths to capture for others to enjoy. 7.<br/>My guess the team of Ryan and Susan (<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=108544" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Magnumphotography</a> and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=59029" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">snaffles</a>) bu could also be <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=116247" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Enlightened</a></td>', 'Wonderful and engaging eyes caught. Boring into my soul! I''d say this was the same bird as another mouse catching entry. Perhaps not as powerful a shot but still technically very good in trying conditions. Wildlife needs to be rewarded especially when we go to these lengths to capture for others to enjoy. 7.My guess the team of Ryan and Susan ( Magnumphotography and  snaffles) bu could also be  Enlightened', '2013-03-05 16:17:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992269, 1055154, 108580, '<td valign="top">Fabulous photography. All just melds together. Light, angle, trees, and the look. 7.</td>', 'Fabulous photography. All just melds together. Light, angle, trees, and the look. 7.', '2013-03-05 16:18:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992273, 1055617, 108580, '<td valign="top">I would hazard a guess this is a Ryan <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=108544" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Magnumphotography</a> shot but could easily be <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=116247" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Enlightened</a>. The intensity of this Owl species eyes is always a drawcard and it was indeed the first thing I noticed, despite the action of the wings and the landing, and then, bam, the mouse opened up a new dimension to the shot. Superb. What on earth a mouse is doing in a dead branch is beyond me, but I understand the skill needed to capture this and get it in focus and keep the bird un-cropped. VWD and will no doubt be Top 10 and possibly Top 3. This is my only 10 of the challenge despite stiff competition but I am biased toward BiF.</td>', 'I would hazard a guess this is a Ryan  Magnumphotography shot but could easily be  Enlightened. The intensity of this Owl species eyes is always a drawcard and it was indeed the first thing I noticed, despite the action of the wings and the landing, and then, bam, the mouse opened up a new dimension to the shot. Superb. What on earth a mouse is doing in a dead branch is beyond me, but I understand the skill needed to capture this and get it in focus and keep the bird un-cropped. VWD and will no doubt be Top 10 and possibly Top 3. This is my only 10 of the challenge despite stiff competition but I am biased toward BiF.', '2013-03-05 16:20:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992274, 1056008, 108580, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image with masterful use of negative space. 8 bumped to 9.</td>', 'Beautiful image with masterful use of negative space. 8 bumped to 9.', '2013-03-05 16:21:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992275, 1054711, 108580, '<td valign="top">Photography at it''s best. Unique and refreshing. Thought provoking; who is the man, who is the woman? Secret liaisons? Sex Scandal?<br/>Of course I believe it has it''s roots in the recent blur challenge and maybe didn''t fit for it''s subtleness in that category, just her head, that no doubt was not, if you''ll pardon the pun, enough to be "in your face". So it made it to the FS! Thank you speed voters for chasing it here. 8 but bumped to a 9.<br/> <br/>I trust there are more images you took during this shoot and would be honoured if you could link me to them post challenge.<br/> <br/>Paul if this is you, you''re indeed a <strike>wizard</strike> master of the modern subtle nude. If not Paul, then naturally I trust you will take that as a compliment.</td>', 'Photography at it''s best. Unique and refreshing. Thought provoking; who is the man, who is the woman? Secret liaisons? Sex Scandal?Of course I believe it has it''s roots in the recent blur challenge and maybe didn''t fit for it''s subtleness in that category, just her head, that no doubt was not, if you''ll pardon the pun, enough to be "in your face". So it made it to the FS! Thank you speed voters for chasing it here. 8 but bumped to a 9. I trust there are more images you took during this shoot and would be honoured if you could link me to them post challenge. Paul if this is you, you''re indeed a wizard master of the modern subtle nude. If not Paul, then naturally I trust you will take that as a compliment.', '2013-03-05 16:21:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6992278, 1053196, 108580, '<td valign="top">Stunning separation and detail. 7</td>', 'Stunning separation and detail. 7', '2013-03-05 16:23:02.000000', NULL, 1),
