(6993031, 1055827, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>Nice moody lighting here. Love the movement trails that are on his dark side. Normally not a fan of so much negative space but it truly works in this composition. I get the sense of movement of him moving from one point in his life to the next. The only thing with the title is I wish there was something within the photograph to give us a visual indication of round or circular. Perhaps if all the movement trails were all in the same curved motion or the wall being curved/rounded. When you can show more within the composition rather than telling it becomes that much more stronger. Still a great photograph.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  Nice moody lighting here. Love the movement trails that are on his dark side. Normally not a fan of so much negative space but it truly works in this composition. I get the sense of movement of him moving from one point in his life to the next. The only thing with the title is I wish there was something within the photograph to give us a visual indication of round or circular. Perhaps if all the movement trails were all in the same curved motion or the wall being curved/rounded. When you can show more within the composition rather than telling it becomes that much more stronger. Still a great photograph.', '2013-03-06 12:23:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6993037, 1055181, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>How neat is that to be able to look outside the window and see living nature outside! You have such great detail in the fur, muzzle and the eyes of the fox but you need to play up those strengths. As it stands now those great details get lost with too much ''negative'' space that does nothing for the composition. Bring me closer to this beautiful animal. I don''t know if you have the large size to do this but I would crop it down to a square crop that starts just a bit above the front leg and gets the whole head with the pine tree as the backdrop. With that closer view your audience will get and appreciate all the great details by coming face to face with this fox.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. How neat is that to be able to look outside the window and see living nature outside! You have such great detail in the fur, muzzle and the eyes of the fox but you need to play up those strengths. As it stands now those great details get lost with too much ''negative'' space that does nothing for the composition. Bring me closer to this beautiful animal. I don''t know if you have the large size to do this but I would crop it down to a square crop that starts just a bit above the front leg and gets the whole head with the pine tree as the backdrop. With that closer view your audience will get and appreciate all the great details by coming face to face with this fox.', '2013-03-06 12:28:56.000000', NULL, 1),
