(6997441, 1054197, 69325, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC! I really like the composition and the cropping on this. These types of street shots are always appealing to me, you did a really nice job seeing the photo opportunity here and capturing a good moment with the subject walking into the frame.<br/> <br/>Don''t be too discouraged over this score, you have found out two important things about DPC with this image. 1: DPC voters have a much more critical eye than voters on most other sites. This is a good thing though, if you are open to criticism your photography will improve by leaps and bounds here. 2: DPC voters are VERY tough on selective desaturation. To me, selective desat is like frosting on a cake, a little is great but too much can make you a little sick :)<br/>If you''re early into learning photography this is something I think most of us go thru, experimenting with different techniques in photoshop. All in all i think there are definitely more positive things than negative. Keep shooting and entering!<br/> <br/>-Jason</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Welcome to DPC! I really like the composition and the cropping on this. These types of street shots are always appealing to me, you did a really nice job seeing the photo opportunity here and capturing a good moment with the subject walking into the frame. Don''t be too discouraged over this score, you have found out two important things about DPC with this image. 1: DPC voters have a much more critical eye than voters on most other sites. This is a good thing though, if you are open to criticism your photography will improve by leaps and bounds here. 2: DPC voters are VERY tough on selective desaturation. To me, selective desat is like frosting on a cake, a little is great but too much can make you a little sick :)If you''re early into learning photography this is something I think most of us go thru, experimenting with different techniques in photoshop. All in all i think there are definitely more positive things than negative. Keep shooting and entering! -Jason', '2013-03-11 21:51:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6997632, 1055154, 68504, '<td valign="top">beautiful, transporting.</td>', 'beautiful, transporting.', '2013-03-12 01:46:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6997634, 1055750, 68504, '<td valign="top">pure synergy. lovely composition, lovely light.</td>', 'pure synergy. lovely composition, lovely light.', '2013-03-12 01:48:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6997668, 1055175, 69325, '<td valign="top">LOL, Well, sorry, it me from the CC again!<br/> <br/>This is another great shot from this series Janine. What I love about this shot is not just the action of the bird that you captured. It''s the shape of the feathers amongst the foliage that makes the bird look like a flower, just briiliant!<br/> <br/>I know the spirit of the Critique Club is to offer some suggestions on things that could be improved in the image but honestly it''s hard to find anything. The only thing that made me wonder is if the blues got pumped up to much in the b/g as it seems to be bleeding onto some of the feathers. But hey, 18th in the free study is nice!<br/> <br/>-J</td>', 'LOL, Well, sorry, it me from the CC again! This is another great shot from this series Janine. What I love about this shot is not just the action of the bird that you captured. It''s the shape of the feathers amongst the foliage that makes the bird look like a flower, just briiliant! I know the spirit of the Critique Club is to offer some suggestions on things that could be improved in the image but honestly it''s hard to find anything. The only thing that made me wonder is if the blues got pumped up to much in the b/g as it seems to be bleeding onto some of the feathers. But hey, 18th in the free study is nice! -J', '2013-03-12 03:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6997716, 1055750, 100831, '<td valign="top">most excellent spellbinder.</td>', 'most excellent spellbinder.', '2013-03-12 07:52:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6998085, 1055939, 69325, '<td valign="top">Hey, Critique Club here :)<br/> <br/>First and foremost this is a great traditional portrait, nice lighting, nice blurred b/g and it fills the frame nicely. I am also a fan of the slight vignette. Also, it''s nice and sharp.<br/> <br/>The only change I would make is what you already noted, a white reflector to bounce some light into the face, especially the eyes, would have done wonders.<br/> <br/>On a side note, I feel like your eyes are penetrating my soul.....<br/> <br/>Keep Shooting!<br/> <br/>J</td>', 'Hey, Critique Club here :) First and foremost this is a great traditional portrait, nice lighting, nice blurred b/g and it fills the frame nicely. I am also a fan of the slight vignette. Also, it''s nice and sharp. The only change I would make is what you already noted, a white reflector to bounce some light into the face, especially the eyes, would have done wonders. On a side note, I feel like your eyes are penetrating my soul..... Keep Shooting! J', '2013-03-12 19:49:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6998230, 1056012, 123833, '<td valign="top">Looking at the wide angle lens you used - do you take your self-portraits while holding the camera in your hands?</td>', 'Looking at the wide angle lens you used - do you take your self-portraits while holding the camera in your hands?', '2013-03-12 22:00:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6998573, 1053871, 117055, '<td valign="top">Beautiful lighting and composition, and you are right, the figure out on the rock really provides great perspective. Congrats!</td>', 'Beautiful lighting and composition, and you are right, the figure out on the rock really provides great perspective. Congrats!', '2013-03-13 03:01:21.000000', NULL, 0),
